insert into public.forum_posts (thread_id, number, author_name, avatar, author_rank, author_post_count, author_online, body, posted_at, posted_tz, edited_at, edit_reason, announcement, provenance) values
  ('ioe-ep1', 1, 'YALBot', 'av-yalbot', 'Moderator', 12482, true, '[b]Episode 1 is now available.[/b]

Please keep discussion focused on Episode 1.
Do not post spoilers for future episodes.
Use spoiler tags for manga/source material discussion.

[small]— Automated post by YALBot. Replies are open.[/small]', '2013-10-05T17:31:00Z', 'JST', null, null, true, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 2, 'xXSoraGauthier_KunXx', 'av-starcircuit', 'Anime Addict', 1348, true, 'Okay WHAT was that ending?? I thought this was gonna be a normal school/sci-fi thing and then Planetation just went full nightmare mode lol. One second they''re picking weapons and posing in the lobby and the next minute YAMAGA284 is ripping into them and the whole map is exploding. The "NO RESTRICTIONS ENABLED" system message had me actually go O_O

Why does this anime not have an OP yet btw, did anyone else''s stream play it at the END', '2013-10-05T17:37:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 3, 'NekoToast92', 'av-nekotoast', 'Forum Regular', 884, true, 'Sora''s voice is way younger than I expected, but it actually fits? He sounds 12 without sounding annoying. That''s rare.

The way he just goes "I hate later" on the rooftop... I felt that in my SOUL not gonna lie ;_;

Also can we talk about how casual he is during the YAMAGA fight? Dude is literally bleeding and just goes "AAARRGGHHHH!!! fight me harder" energy. We have a scrappy-young-hero-archetype protag on our hands :3', '2013-10-05T17:39:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 4, 'NodeCorePilot', 'av-mecharonin', 'Senior Member', 2201, true, 'The weapons look RIDICULOUS in the best way:

[list]
[*][b]MetaCode[/b] — arm that turns into a blade AND fires bullets AND burst-steps. of course Sora gets the kitchen-sink weapon
[*][b]Crucible Dual Blades[/b] — remote controlled flying greatswords with IGNITION mode. Grayson''s flaming herding combo was sick
[*][b]Flame Guns[/b] — dual machine guns + grapple + jet pack. Abigail aiming the dual flame gunss like she''s already tired of everyone''s nonsense got me XD
[*][b]NodeCore[/b] — ben choosing to DISABLE the safety governors WITHIN 30 SECONDS of getting it is the most accurate "this guy" character writing I''ve seen all year
[/list]

This is so 2010s mecha-anime coded. Im in.', '2013-10-05T17:44:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 5, 'PlanetationBro', 'av-bluesoda', 'Senior Member', 1902, true, 'Sora''s voice sounds younger than I expected. The VA was Mariya Ise right :ooo

Also can we talk about the cold open?? That whole sequence with the BABY in the blue egg under the World Tree, then the eye-snap-open and the colors flipping to bruised cyan and lilac-gray for 8 frames, then the static shockwave??? Bruh I had to pause and rewind. Then they cut to suburban morning alarm clock "hi I''m Sora" like nothing happened.

They are NOT being subtle about this mattering later.', '2013-10-05T17:51:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 6, 'ShounenLifer_VHS', 'av-vhssamurai', 'Anime Addict', 4177, false, 'Animation had some rough TV spots (the hallway riot inbetweens were noticeably stiff in a few places, especially when Ben was sliding past the trash can) but the action cuts had ENERGY. The white-flash transition into Sora vs YAMAGA284 with the cinematic black bars dropping in was unironically one of the cleanest presentation choices I''ve seen in a fall season opener.

I''ll take that over shiny lifeless sakuga any day. Studio''s leaning into the "early 2010s game-anime" feel hard with all the UI overlays and combat logs and it actually WORKS instead of feeling cluttered. Nobody''s done MMO-overlay-as-comedy this clean in years iirc.', '2013-10-05T18:04:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 7, 'GraysonSus_NotSus', 'av-kiranotkira', 'Forum Regular', 612, true, 'Grayson is either going to be my favorite or the most suspicious guy in the room. No in-between.

He''s the only one who:

[list]
[*]Actually read the pre-release lore
[*]Knows where Frontier Risk Management is
[*]Stays calm when YAMAGA284 dives him
[*]Has the calmest "Don''t die out there, okay?" line at the train station
[/list]

That is either "best friend hero archetype" or "season 2 traitor reveal" and I genuinely refuse to predict which one.', '2013-10-05T18:08:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 8, 'PlanetationKid', 'av-planetkid', 'Newbie', 23, true, 'Nope. That storm at the end is NOT part of the game. Calling it now.

The system going "STATUS: UNCONFIRMED VIRUS MANIFESTATION" over by KO HQ and Nova straight up saying "too many lives have been lost" while the player counter ticks down in real time? That is not normal patch behavior lmao. Gamlet up there betting on these kids while a virus eats the World Tree is the most early-2010s anime setup ever.

Also why is the threat marker pulsing on Sora''s HUD reflecting the EXACT same red pulse from KO''s wall display, that''s not framing they do for nothing', '2013-10-05T18:12:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 9, 'BurstAnimKid', 'av-luckynoodle', 'Member', 244, true, 'Abigail already best girl and it has been ONE episode.

The "…Barbaracy?" face after Miyuki''s speech, the way she just shows up with the flame guns grapple to slash YAMAGA284 mid-air after Sora softened him up, AND that little moment where she clutches her blue necklace pendant after rolling on the ground — like the show is showing you something matters without underlining it.

I''m not taking criticism at this time :P', '2013-10-05T18:20:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 10, '3EpisodeRule', 'av-3eprule', 'Senior Member', 1508, false, 'This premiere was messy but interesting. I''m giving it the 3 episode rule.

If it explains half of what it threw at us — the baby/egg cold open, why a "beginner trial" has zero restrictions, what KO actually does, what Frontier Risk Management is going to be, why the storm threat is named ??? — I''m in for the cour.

If episode 2 is just more lobby chatter and Ben yelling, I''m out. Calling it neutral until then.', '2013-10-05T18:27:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 11, 'likko-chwangun213', 'av-sakurastatic', 'Forum Regular', 723, true, 'That cold open is gonna live rent-free in my head until next week.

Like. The Verdant Expanse with the half-broken watchforts, the wind sounding wrong (someone said it was "dragging like breath through a broken speaker" and I''ll never unhear it), the BABY HAND pressing the glass of the egg, and then the EYE OPEN shockwave with the colors going all bruised and lilac-gray for 8 frames??? That was straight up a horror short.

And then BAM, suburban morning alarm clock "hi I''m Sora let''s go to school." I''m gonna be thinking about this opener all week T_T

If THAT is what''s actually in the World Tree under Planetation I am scared and excited at the same time', '2013-10-05T18:33:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 12, 'SakugaThreadZero', 'av-zeroframe', 'Database Contributor', 5882, true, '[quote=PlanetationBro;5]Sora''s voice sounds younger than I expected. The VA was Mariya Ise right :ooo[/quote]

Yeah same. I thought they''d give him a deeper voice from the promo art, but the younger voice makes the danger feel worse somehow.

Because they were coming off Sinful Apex that''s why. Pretty different role obviously, but you can hear the same actor energy in the way they handle the rooftop monologue — that quiet "I hate later" delivery is a Mariya Ise specialty.

Confirmed cast on the JP listing btw:

[small][list]
[*]Sora Gauthier — Mariya Ise
[*]Grayson Rothenberg — Nobuhiko Okamoto
[*]Abigail June — Kana Hanazawa
[*]Ben Smythe — Kaito Ishikawa
[*]Miyuki Kagemitsu (Hammond Council 1, President) — Saori Hayami
[*]Echo Desmond (Hammond Council 1, Vice President) — Rina Satou
[*]William Jones (Hammond Council 1, Supervisor) — Hiro Shimono
[*]Kieran Atsushi (Hammond Council 1, Advisor) — Hiroshi Kamiya
[*]Likko Valenne (Hammond Council 1, Secretary) — Ayane Sakura
[*]Gamlet (FRM assistant) — Kishou Taniyama
[*]Nova (FRM assistant) — Yui Ishikawa
[*]Michael Pentulengro — Yoshimasa Hosoya
[*]Andreas Walker — Tasuku Hatanaka
[/list][/small]

Hammond Council 1 = Miyuki''s squad. so the entire squad in the lobby scene is fully credited and stacked. Rina Satou, Hiro Shimono, Hiroshi Kamiya, AND Ayane Sakura supporting Saori Hayami in one squad. that is an absurd voice lineup.

(also — the surname combo Desmond / Jones / Atsushi / Valenne on a Japanese-broadcast school anime is wild. the show''s clearly going for that "international academy" vibe even with kanji-coded characters mixed in. and Pentulengro / Walker as side names too — this is going hard on the international thing.)', '2013-10-05T18:41:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 13, 'ImageboardGoblin', 'av-forumgoblin', 'Anime Addict', 3402, false, 'Manga reader here. Pay attention to the storm. Pay attention to who shows up at Frontier Risk Management. The narrator''s "someone… appears" line at the end is doing a lot of heavy lifting for what''s coming. That''s all I''ll say.

The anime''s pacing this stuff out about how I expected, just don''t blink during the Verdant Expanse cuts >:)', '2013-10-05T18:48:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 14, 'NovaFanPixel', 'av-moonlitpixel', 'Database Contributor', 6210, true, '@ImageboardGoblin Bro use spoiler tags properly next time. The whole point of the rule in YALBot''s pinned post is so anime-only watchers can talk freely. Even saying "pay attention to X" counts as a tease. Like this:

[spoiler=manga readers only]Manga reader here too, not saying anything specific, but yeah, pay attention to the storm. There''s also a small moment with Abigail''s necklace this episode that pays off a LOT later. Just enjoy ep 1 anime-only people, you''ll know when it hits.[/spoiler]

It''s not hard. Mods please >_>', '2013-10-05T18:55:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 15, 'AbigailFanAlready', 'av-abigailfan', 'Newbie', 4, true, 'NEW ACCOUNT JUST TO POST IN THIS THREAD I''M NOT KIDDING

Abigail (Saturn12 in-game btw) is exactly what this kind of squad needed. She''s the only one who isn''t dropping IQ for the bit and she still has the best comedic timing in the whole class. The "Oh yeah, they''re loud, annoying… Retards?" deadpan at the vending machine had me ROFL. cool, funny, relatable, loyal, best girl of 2013, I''m not making it up.

[b]Now let''s talk about the FINISHER. because somebody at Burst drew that.[/b]

let me actually walk through the frame work:

[list]
[*][b]frame 1[/b] — she''s launching off the moving cart, hook fires off-screen first (that''s the BANG you hear before you see her), gas line venting in a sharp downward burst that you can read as a tiny silhouette
[*][b]frame 2-4[/b] — she''s airborne, full body rotation through the camera-whip, her hair is animated separately from her uniform from her grapple line, three layers of motion happening at once, all individually drawn
[*][b]frame 5[/b] — the flame guns blades start glowing that orange-yellow ignition. that''s a CUSTOM color pass for her specifically. Grayson''s Crucible glow is red-orange. Abigail''s is gold-orange. the show is COLOR-CODING the girls'' weapon energy so it reads instantly different from the boys'' even in chaotic frames
[*][b]frame 6-8[/b] — she plants the hook on the open body, dives in, and the slashes are drawn as overlapping continuous arcs instead of standard impact frames. that''s MORE work, not less. that''s somebody saying "Abigail''s kill cam will not look like Grayson''s"
[*][b]frame 9[/b] — the explosion, but the camera holds on HER body language: she can''t find a clean landing area, she rolls instead of sticking the landing, dirt in her hair. it''s the most lived-in finisher animation I''ve seen all year
[*][b]and then the moment that broke me[/b] — mid-fall, she clutches her blue necklace pendant subconsciously, lands, then realizes it''s still there, and SIGHS. quietly. that''s a personal beat carved into a kill cam. you don''t draw that unless you''re writing her like a person.
[/list]

that''s not just sakuga budget. that''s somebody at the script + storyboard layer going "Abigail isn''t decoration, she''s the one who finishes the fight, and she gets ONE small private gesture inside the loudest moment of the episode." that''s [b]Natsuki Takuya''s[/b] whole philosophy on writing women in one shot — loud combat, quiet interior life, no fan-service framing, the camera respects her even in motion.

compare that to how a generic 2013 action-anime would have drawn this same moment: low-angle skirt shot during the air rotation, dramatic chest pant after landing, breathy "...did I do that?" line read. Burst drew the OPPOSITE of that, deliberately. the camera stays at her face. the necklace clutch is the emotional payoff, not her body.

"...How did that happen?" hits 10x harder when you realize the storyboard team made a CHOICE to give her that line at that angle.

I might be biased. I might be VERY biased. I do not care. Hanazawa was BORN to voice this character.', '2013-10-05T19:06:00Z', 'JST', '2013-10-05T19:11:00Z', 'typo, fixed her in-game name (Saturn12 not Saturn-12). also added the frame breakdown because I rewatched the cut 6 more times.', false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 16, 'TokuFanMango', 'av-robomango', 'Forum Regular', 612, true, 'Real talk: the YAMAGA284 fight is what sold me on this show.

Grayson''s flaming Crucible Blades in the first half — the way one blade circles high like a predator wing while the other carves low to herd the enemy line into bad footing — that''s not just sakuga, that''s CHOREOGRAPHY. Then Sora cuts in with under-mastered MetaCode and you can FEEL him learning the rhythm mid-combat.

The way the "YAMAGA READ LEVEL: 100%" UI drops to 30% when he stops attacking the same way is such a clean way to show "he''s not stronger, he''s getting smarter." Like seriously, that little number changing on screen is doing more emotional work than 90% of "training arc" episodes. Then Abigail cleans up.

Squad-fight choreo of the season already imo. I was genuinely hyped. I haven''t been this hyped at a fight in a premiere in years.', '2013-10-05T19:14:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 17, 'KaichouEnjoyer', 'av-kaichouenjoyer', 'Anime Addict', 2118, true, 'Miyuki getting the "no fear, no hesitation, no regrets" speech AT THE START of episode 1 is wild.

Most shows would save that for ep 6 minimum. Then the way she just smugly chooses Void Rift like "so is grass green then?" and Echo, Likko, Kieran and William all confirm one by one while their player count rolls 1,284 → 1,347... that''s such a cool way to show "this is a different team, they''re already a unit."

[b]The animation on her speech alone needs a separate award category.[/b] let me try to actually describe it:

Burst doesn''t do the easy thing here. they don''t push in for a close-up. they don''t tilt the camera up to make her look bigger. they HOLD ON A WIDE THE WHOLE TIME and let her stillness do the work. the only thing that moves for the first three lines of her speech is her HAIR — individually animated against the data tower wind — while her body stays completely composed. then when she hits "[i]If the walls above stand in front of you, advance to crush them![/i]" the camera ALMOST imperceptibly drops by maybe 2-3 pixels per second, building a slow looming effect WITHOUT cutting. that''s a hand-drawn camera move done with care over a full 8-second hold. that''s effort. that''s a key animator going "no, this is the shot, we''re not cheating it with a still."

and her body language at "[i]Therefore, our choice towards history is refusal![/i]" — she doesn''t raise her voice, she LOWERS it, while the OST swells underneath. she crosses her arms more tightly. the smug "so is grass green then?" frown softens at the corner of her mouth for ONE FRAME. that''s the kind of micro-expression you draw on purpose. that''s a character animator who studied her.

this is exactly what [b]Natsuki Takuya[/b] is known for in the original manga: women whose authority comes from stillness, not from being framed as "intimidating." Burst translated that to anime with FULL respect for the source.

"Those pigs can have whatever''s left." Excuse me?? Class president of all time. I''m calling it: we are getting a Council vs Main Crew arc and I am READY. and when Miyuki finally goes off in combat, given how restrained they''re drawing her right now, the eventual release is going to be NUCLEAR.

Also "Barbaracy" might be the funniest fake-formal word an anime has ever invented. Abigail''s whole face turning into spiritual disgust was peak comedic timing — and crucially, the animators drew BOTH girls full-frame in that beat, no cheating with off-screen reactions. they wanted you to see both performances at once.', '2013-10-05T19:22:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 18, 'sleepySenpai_DesuKa', 'av-sleepysenpai', 'Forum Regular', 933, false, 'the OP not playing till the END of the episode is such a power move

