  ('ioe-ep1', 53, 'HellsKitchenAnimu', 'av-millenniumfan', 'Forum Regular', 503, true, 'I''m putting my flag down right here, right now: [b]Grayson is the season 1 traitor.[/b]

he "happened" to read the pre-release lore. he "happens" to know where Frontier Risk Management is. he stays calm during YAMAGA. he gives Sora a quiet "Don''t die out there, okay?" at the train station like he KNOWS Sora is about to walk into something. he is too convenient. the show is setting him up.

if I''m wrong I''ll eat my keyboard.', '2013-10-06T01:08:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 54, 'KaichouEnjoyer', 'av-kaichouenjoyer', 'Anime Addict', 2123, true, '[quote=HellsKitchenAnimu;53]Grayson is the season 1 traitor.[/quote]

nope. you''re chasing the wrong red herring.

the OBVIOUS antagonist setup is Miyuki. she''s the class president of an authoritarian school. she gave the "no fear, no hesitation, no regrets" speech at the START of ep 1, which is wild placement. she chose Void Rift with "those pigs can have whatever''s left." she literally runs an entire student council squad that''s already several levels ahead. all signs point to her.

...which is why Miyuki is NOT the antagonist either. shows don''t telegraph their villain that hard in ep 1. she''s gonna be the rival who eventually allies. the REAL antagonist is the one we haven''t met yet. probably the "someone... appears" the narrator teased at the end.

