  ('ioe-ep1', 55, 'DrowsyGhostVHS', 'av-kitchenstar', 'Member', 421, true, 'not sure if anyone''s said this yet but the colorblind-shockwave moment in the cold open is doing something specific.

red-orange → bruised cyan. green → dead nicotine-yellow. skin → cold lilac-gray. blue → electric cobalt with white core.

that''s not random. it''s a chromatic INVERSION. complementary color palette. when an artist does that, it''s "this is the same world, viewed wrong." like the world is being looked at from the OPPOSITE side. so wherever the baby is, it''s not just a different time. it''s a different ANGLE on the same place.

okay maybe I''m reaching. but my cinema studies degree had to be useful for something.', '2013-10-06T01:35:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 56, 'NodeCorePilot', 'av-mecharonin', 'Senior Member', 2205, true, 'coming back in to talk weapons because it''s all I want to talk about.

The MetaCode tooltip line "Pain feedback: disabled. Impact feedback: reduced." is doing some quiet horror work. It explicitly tells you the SYSTEM is the thing protecting players from feeling damage. when the storm/virus eats the system... what happens to that protection? Sora gets cut by YAMAGA284 and BLEEDS. he says "AAARRGGHHH!!!" That bleed could be cosmetic. or the system could already be slipping.

also Ben disabling his NodeCore safety governors before he''s used the device once is so "this guy will absolutely lose a limb in episode 8" energy.', '2013-10-06T01:48:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 57, 'OkamotoAcolyte', 'av-ciphercaramel', 'Forum Regular', 1108, true, 'HOLD ON. HOLD ON. HOLD ON.

