  ('ioe-ep1', 58, 'StormWallTheory', 'av-stormwalltheory', 'Senior Member', 3019, true, '[quote=HellsKitchenAnimu;53]Grayson is the season 1 traitor.[/quote]

I disagree but I love the energy. for what it''s worth my read on Grayson is "high-agency tactician who is loyal by [i]choice[/i], not by need". the lore-reading isn''t sinister and it isn''t insecurity either — it''s deliberate. he''s the kid who shows up READY because he [i]wants[/i] to be the one holding the team''s structure. the dual-blade work in the YAMAGA fight is the tell: he''s not flailing, he''s running zones, controlling space, and trusting Sora to be the closer. that''s a confident fighter, not an anxious one.

the train station "Don''t die out there, okay?" hits different when you read him that way. it''s not foreshadowing AND it''s not anxiety. it''s a controlled, intentional thing said to a friend by a kid who has decided, on purpose, to be the steady one in the group. that''s an actual choice he made before ep 1 even started. the show is just letting us notice it.

the redacted KO Tier 3 tag means he''s carrying weight nobody else in the squad knows about. but he''s carrying it on purpose. that''s not a traitor setup. that''s a backstory the show is going to peel apart slowly — and the reveal is going to be the opposite of "secretly evil." it''s going to be "of course he was always like this and we just didn''t have the context."

(but also if I''m wrong I''ll buy you a new keyboard.)', '2013-10-06T02:18:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 59, 'SonOfTheToaster', 'av-calsparrow', 'Newbie', 17, true, 'NekoToast92, HollowToast, ShadowToast.

this is a toaster forum now.', '2013-10-06T02:31:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 60, 'MillenniumAnimeFan2001', 'av-calsparrow', 'Newbie', 52, true, 'second rewatch in. a few more notes that aren''t theories, just appreciation.

1. The way Sora hands his finished essay to the teacher and JUST LEAVES without grabbing his stuff. he doesn''t even bring his binder to the rooftop. he came to write the essay, the rooftop wasn''t planned. that''s a small character beat that says a lot.
2. Abigail''s necklace clutch when she''s falling after killing YAMAGA. she doesn''t look at it dramatically. she just GRABS it and exhales. that''s a "this matters but I don''t want anyone to see me caring" kind of beat.
3. The "Don''t die out there, okay?" / "I won''t." exchange between Grayson and Sora. that''s the LAST line before Sora''s solo skateboard ride home, which the show makes a whole sequence out of with him riding into evening. the show is doing setup work in dialogue you don''t notice until you''re looking for it.

this episode is dense but not careless. ok now I''ll shut up. see you on page 4.', '2013-10-06T03:14:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 61, 'BurstAnimKid', 'av-luckynoodle', 'Member', 251, true, 'Abigail update: still best girl. updated my desktop wallpaper to the necklace clutch frame. don''t @ me.

also y''all are SLEEPING on Abigail''s "I''d rather hang out with real people, like Lisa" line at the vending machine. she''s not above the world, she just has standards. that''s the strongest "she''s already above all of you idiots" energy and I am here for it.', '2013-10-06T03:31:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 62, 'HypeBeam_3500', 'av-okamoto', 'Member', 178, true, 'just got out of class watched it on lunch break HOLY-

okay I have to be honest. that YAMAGA284 fight was [b]BLOODY FANTASTIC.[/b] I mean that in every single sense of the word. literal blood. literal chaos. literal "I have to pause and breathe" energy. Burst said "you want choreography? we have CHOREOGRAPHY" and they did NOT come to play.

let me recap the bloodbath in order:

[list]
[*]Grayson igniting the Crucible Dual Blades, herding YAMAGA284 with one blade HIGH like a predator wing and the other carving LOW, throwing close-range punch flurries IN BETWEEN the blade passes. blood on his knuckles by the second exchange. catches a sniper round on the flat of a returning blade and GRINS through the spark shower.
[*]Sora getting CUT — like actual blood on the grass cut — spitting blood, no speech, just breathing, then AAARRGGHHH-charging back in with an unmastered burst step. dirt in his mouth. fire in his eyes. punches the flank. SMASH.
[*]ABIGAIL''S FINISHER. she LAUNCHES off the moving cart. orange-yellow flame guns blades. mid-air rotation. plants the hook on the open body, dives in, slashes at NEAR-CONTACT range. BOOOM. YAMAGA''s armor EXPLODES. red blood explodes out of the body. center-frame "K.O!" text. necklace pendant clutch on the landing roll.
[/list]

and before anyone starts with the "the guys fought, Abigail supported" reading: NO. absolutely not. this episode is not doing "male dominate, female support." Abigail does not arrive as backup flavor. she arrives as the decisive finisher. Eden is putting its girls in the center of the action language and daring us to notice.

I have to know. who had it best in that fight??

[b]TEAM GRAYSON[/b] — chess work, tactical herding, IGNITION mode
[b]TEAM SORA[/b] — 1v1 spite, READ LEVEL meltdown, MetaCode awakening
[b]TEAM ABIGAIL[/b] — the finisher, the launch, the necklace, the explosion, the actual "this fight is OVER" authority

I''m flagging TEAM ABIGAIL personally because her part was genuinely [b]INSANE.[/b] and because Eden''s girls are clearly not side garnish. they''re core. maybe MORE core than the boys if the show keeps boarding them like this. running back to math. don''t break the thread without me.', '2013-10-06T03:42:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 63, 'PixelMomo', 'av-rawrxd', 'Newbie', 5, true, '[quote=HypeBeam_3500 — #62 (this page)]I have to know. who had it best in that fight?? TEAM GRAYSON / TEAM SORA / TEAM ABIGAIL[/quote]

ABIGAIL. FINISHED. HIM. lmaoooooooo

[b]TEAM ABIGAIL.[/b] case closed. coffin closed. YAMAGA''s actual BODY exploded in red, and nobody else got a kill cam that ended on a center-frame "K.O!" text card. she had the ONLY kill in the fight. she gets the W.

also I am begging people to stop calling this "she cleaned up after the boys." that''s exactly the lazy reading Eden is pushing against. Grayson controls space. Sora breaks the pattern. Abigail ENDS the encounter. that''s not support. that''s command position. the final punctuation mark belongs to her.

continue arguing if you want. I''ll be in the corner replaying her hook launch on slow-mo. somebody at Burst earned their paycheck on that one cut alone. TEAM ABIGAIL is not a joke option, it''s the thesis.', '2013-10-06T03:48:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 64, 'KaichouEnjoyer', 'av-kaichouenjoyer', 'Anime Addict', 2127, true, 'Miyuki appreciation post incoming.

