still cautious. but warmer than I was 5 hours ago. fine, give me ep 2.', '2013-10-06T04:38:00Z', 'JST', '2013-10-06T04:42:00Z', 'rewatched, softening', false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 68, 'DeluxeSenpai_99', 'av-calsparrow', 'Newbie', 4, true, '[b]ANIMATION POST — Burst really animated this on a DEBUT.[/b]

I want to say this cleanly because I keep seeing people undersell it: [i]this is some of the best looking ep 1 animation I''ve seen in years.[/i] Genuinely. Not "good for ep 1." Just [i]good[/i].

Receipts:

[list]
[*]Silhouette readability across the entire YAMAGA fight — you can pause on any frame and instantly read who''s where, who''s attacking, who''s defending. That''s layout discipline. Okado''s [i]Neon Afterimage[/i] training is showing.
[*]The lobby weapon-reveal sequence has more clean held poses than entire ARCS of other shows.
[*]The compositing where the lobby UI bleeds into the action layers without ever feeling cluttered — that''s Ninagawa-tier comp work and it''s only ep 1.
[*]Camera that behaves like an animator''s camera (cuts on emotion, not on coverage) instead of a generic game cinematic camera. That''s Suzuhara on storyboards earning her credit.
[/list]

And Burst is a brand new studio. [b]Their DEBUT show.[/b] They''re already animating circles around shows that have been running for a decade. [i]WHAT.[/i]

I kept pausing on random frames this whole episode and they all read clean. That''s the test. They passed it twenty times in 22 minutes.', '2013-10-06T04:51:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 69, 'ShounenLifer_VHS', 'av-vhssamurai', 'Anime Addict', 4184, true, 'I want to call out a moment that''s getting overlooked: the UI nameplate on the homeroom teacher.

"HOMEROOM TEACHER — LV. ???" then it FLICKERS through "??? → TEACHER → ADMIN → SYSTEM OVERRIDE". that''s such a SMART joke. she didn''t get angry, she just walked in and the whole room shut up. the UI tried to label her like an enemy and failed because she doesn''t fit the category. anyone who''s been in a real classroom knows that exact teacher.

then the room goes silent and the buffering icon glitches in. peak comedy that needs zero dialogue.', '2013-10-06T05:06:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
