[*]YAMAGA fight: heavy percussion + electric guitar layers. peak
[*]OP at the end: T.M.Revolution. nuff said
[/list]

credits scroll wasn''t long enough to read everything. I want a full OST CD release yesterday.', '2013-10-06T07:04:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 79, 'Nova_Is_The_Boss', 'av-bostonbean', 'Member', 514, true, 'I want to push back on the early-thread takes that read Nova and Gamlet as a "shipping" scene. that''s flattening her and I''m not having it.

watch the coffee beat again. Gamlet says "did you put honey in here?" and Nova answers "well, I always knew you liked it, so." Burst frames it where Nova is STANDING, holding the tray, and Gamlet is SEATED. she is physically above him in the shot. he sips his coffee. she has already moved on to checking the player counter. that''s not a romance beat. that''s an "I run this office and I keep track of every detail in it including what my boss takes in his coffee" beat. that''s [b]workplace competence[/b], drawn with care.

then the dread hits and Nova delivers "It''s over." into the silence. and again: SHE''S the one who diagnoses the world ending. Gamlet is the one who reacts to her diagnosis. she''s THE source of truth in that office.

then Nova drops the second thesis statement of the episode: "we have to take a stand. even if we''re all morally wrong." that''s the show''s central moral argument and Burst gave it to NOVA, not to Gamlet. she is the closest thing the adult-world has to a captain in this episode. Gamlet is great. Kishou Taniyama owns that performance. but Nova IS the office.

if you''re going to ship them — fine, it''s the internet — at least ship her UP not sideways. Nova is not "Gamlet''s anything." Gamlet is "Nova''s boss in name only." that''s the dynamic. write it correctly.

Yui Ishikawa is going to make Nova one of the most respected female adult characters of the season. plant this flag with me.', '2013-10-06T07:18:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 80, 'SakugaThreadZero', 'av-zeroframe', 'Database Contributor', 5891, true, 'checking back in. updating staff credits I missed earlier from the BD pre-release listing:

[list]
[*][b]Director:[/b] Kaihatsu Miura
[*][b]Series Composition / Head Writer:[/b] Keito Kisaragi
[*][b]Storyboard & Pacing Lead:[/b] Tomoe Suzuhara
[*][b]Character Designer / Chief Animation Director:[/b] Lio Haraguchi
[*][b]Art Director (Backgrounds & Settings):[/b] Naochi Sumikuro
[*][b]Colour Designer:[/b] Mirai Kanzaki
[*][b]Sound Director / Audio Editor:[/b] Aoi Tachikaze
[*][b]Music Composer:[/b] Main: Hiroyuki Sawano
[*][b]Action Choreographer:[/b] Yusuke Kagura
[*][b]OP:[/b] "Human x Inhuman" by Takanori Nishikawa (T.M.Revolution)
[*][b]ED:[/b] not yet revealed (no ED played in ep 1, possibly debuts ep 2)
[*][b]Studio:[/b] [b]Burst[/b] (new studio — spun out of Flow Pictures'' late-era cinematic unit, the same staff culture that did [i]Sinful Apex[/i])
[*][b]Original Concept:[/b] original anime, no LN/manga
[/list]

that''s a stacked staff for what''s supposed to be a DEBUT studio. let''s actually go through it because the names are crazy:

[list]
[*][b]Kaihatsu Miura[/b] directing — the [i]Zero Latitude[/i] guy. AND [i]Destiny/Infinite[/i]. AND he co-directed [i]Skyfall Chronicle: Black Aegis[/i]. that''s a "no padding" director. explains why ep 1 felt this dense.
[*][b]Keito Kisaragi[/b] on series comp — head writer on [i]Blizzard Requiem[/i], series comp on [i]Pale Garden Reverie[/i]. emotional through-lines + political tension is exactly her register. that''s why the school chaos AND the rooftop monologue both land.
[*][b]Tomoe Suzuhara[/b] on storyboards — she did the [i]Zero Latitude[/i] long-take and the [i]River of Sparks[/i] alley fights. THAT''S who boarded the YAMAGA284 fight. it makes sense now, the silhouette work is ridiculous.
[*][b]Lio Haraguchi[/b] on character design + chief AD — the [i]Garden of Cinders[/i] OVA crew. faces stay on-model in chaos, that''s their whole thing.
[*][b]Hiroyuki Sawano[/b] on music — obvious in retrospect. the way the bass drops out completely on the rooftop and then SLAMS back in for the YAMAGA fight is textbook Sawano dynamics.
[*][b]Yusuke Kagura[/b] on action choreo — [i]River of Sparks[/i] and [i]Iron Halo Brigade[/i]. tactical-readable fights guy. that''s why YAMAGA''s READ LEVEL drop felt earned and not just a UI prop.
[/list]

and Burst being a brand new studio is wild. their founding staff is basically the Flow Pictures cinematic unit that wrapped [i]Sinful Apex[/i], then split off into their own banner. Eden is their DEBUT show?? what a swing for a launch project. I''m glued to this season now.', '2013-10-06T07:30:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 81, 'NekoToast92', 'av-nekotoast', 'Forum Regular', 892, true, 'I just got home from school and this thread has FOUR more pages than when I left. how do you all do this. I missed the entire MetaCode/storm/Grayson-traitor argument arc.

also for the toaster forum joke on page 3: I am proud to be a founding toaster. NekoToast forever. accept no imitators.', '2013-10-06T07:45:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 82, 'EchoDesmond_VP4Life', 'av-okamoto', 'Member', 728, true, 'EST trash here. it''s 4am, I just rewatched ep 1 for the third time, and I have to write the Echo Desmond post nobody is writing yet. she is being treated as "the third girl on Council 1" and she is so much MORE than that. let me cook.

[b]ECHO DESMOND — HAMMOND COUNCIL 1 VICE PRESIDENT — VA: RINA SATOU[/b]

[b]1. Introduction as motion.[/b] we meet Echo while she is parkouring between two training rails testing dual blades. Burst did not introduce her standing still. they did not introduce her in a static portrait. they introduced her IN motion. that''s not just a stylistic flex — that''s the show telling you "this character''s identity is movement." she does not exist as a pose. she exists as a verb.

[b]2. The parkour is animated CORRECTLY.[/b] weight transfers properly between her feet. her shoulders compensate for her hips. her hair physics lag a beat behind her head turns instead of moving in sync. her dual blades have separate motion arcs because she''s HOLDING them, not posing with them. nobody at Burst said "let''s make her look graceful." somebody said "let''s make her look like an athlete." those are different objectives and the second one is harder.

[b]3. No fan-service framing during the parkour.[/b] camera is held at chest-height in three-quarter view. no low-angle. no zoom on legs. no skirt physics. she''s wearing standard student-council gear with no costume tricks. Burst could have done the lazy thing and they refused. that''s a deliberate storyboarding choice from [b]Tomoe Suzuhara[/b] and it''s a CHOICE.

[b]4. Rina Satou''s "Confirmed. Void Rift."[/b] two words. flat tone. no flirty lilt. no breathy delivery. just clipped pro-soldier confirmation while she''s leaning over the rail grinning into the lobby. that''s the same "I have done this a hundred times" energy you hear in a senior squad lead. Rina Satou is reading Echo as a VETERAN.

[b]5. Body language in the squad shot.[/b] Miyuki is in the center delivering the speech. Echo is staged DIRECTLY BEHIND her right shoulder. that''s the "second-in-command" frame from any military or action genre. Burst put her there on purpose. she''s the VP of Council 1 in fiction AND in staging.

[b]6. The dual blades.[/b] Echo''s blades are smaller, lighter, paired weapons. Grayson gets long single Crucible blades. Abigail gets a grappling pistol. Miyuki gets Zantetsuken. each character''s weapon is BUILT for their body and their movement style. Echo''s weapon is built for SPEED and MOBILITY which matches her parkour intro. that''s character design at the weapon level. nobody at Burst was lazy about Echo.

[b]7. The character grin.[/b] Rina Satou voices the small grin Echo gives during the lobby exposition. she''s having FUN. she''s not stressed. she''s not nervous. she''s not anxious about the upcoming match. she''s amped. that''s an athlete''s pregame face. that''s how you write a confident character without making her arrogant.

Echo Desmond is going to be the breakout of this season for anyone who wasn''t already locked in on Miyuki or Abigail. Rina Satou + this design + this much motion attention = a character who''s going to OWN her own action set piece by ep 4 or 5. plant this flag. quote me later.

respect Echo. she''s earning it in every frame she''s on screen and she''s only been on screen for like 90 seconds.', '2013-10-05T17:31:00Z', 'EDT', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 83, 'LisaSarah_Squad', 'av-bostonbean', 'Member', 256, true, 'okay before this page 5 turns into another "but Sora though" loop, I want to plant a flag for the girls who are NOT in fights this episode and are STILL doing the work:

[b]LISA NEMA-OYUNAA[/b] — the FIRST person in the classroom riot scene to [i]name[/i] what''s actually happening. while everyone else is yelling, Lisa is the one who says "they''re not playing fair, this isn''t a fight, it''s a SHOOT." she''s diagnosing the situation in real time. that''s a strategist brain. she''s the one Ben goes to FIRST when he''s spiraling, and she''s the one who tells him sit down and breathe. Lisa is the squad''s anchor and the show is already telling us so.

[b]SARAH[/b] — the second the cafeteria mob escalates Sarah is on her phone CALLING somebody. who is she calling? we don''t know yet. but the staging shows her actively trying to fix the situation while two boys around her are yelling about how unfair it is. Sarah is doing crisis management at AGE TWELVE. and she does it without raising her voice. that''s a lead-level character trait.

[b]ABIGAIL JUNE[/b] — everyone is talking (correctly) about her grapple finisher but I want to highlight her BEFORE the fight. Abigail is the one who walks INTO the school riot calm. she doesn''t pick up a weapon, doesn''t run away, doesn''t escalate. she just [i]moves through it[/i] with her hands in her hoodie pockets. that staging is intentional. the chaos breaks AROUND her. Abigail is being drawn as un-rattle-able. THAT''S who you want anchoring your team. that''s why the grapple finisher hit later — Burst already taught you in act 1 that Abigail is who stays calm when everyone else loses it.

three girls. zero major fight scenes between them in the first half of the episode. all three of them are STILL the most composed people on screen during the chaos. then Abigail goes on to end the YAMAGA fight.

this is what people mean when they say "Eden writes women like leads." it''s not just the action beats. it''s the WAY the camera trusts them to anchor scenes the boys are losing their minds in. Lisa thinks. Sarah acts. Abigail endures. and then ends the threat.

respect the sane girls. they''re the spine of this team.', '2013-10-06T08:08:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 84, '3EpisodeRule', 'av-3eprule', 'Senior Member', 1524, true, '[quote=StormWallTheory — #74 (page 4)]STORM IS SORA. STORM IS SORA. STORM IS SORA.[/quote]

