  ('ioe-ep1', 90, 'Frontier_Risk_Mgmt', 'av-shadowtoast', 'Newbie', 1, true, 'made an account so I could have this name before anyone else gets it. you''re welcome. checking out, see you ep 2.', '2013-10-06T09:35:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 91, 'PlanetationBro', 'av-bluesoda', 'Senior Member', 1914, true, 'thinking about the theme again.

the show keeps pairing CIVILIAN normalcy with VIOLENCE without bridging them with a transition. school day ↔ trial of war. vending machine joke ↔ flaming dual blades. Ben''s "kiss my ass" energy ↔ Sora getting cut by YAMAGA. it WANTS to feel disorienting.

that''s the texture. the show is putting you inside Sora''s head — a 12 year old who keeps oscillating between "this is just a normal day" and "I am IN something." the rooftop monologue is the only place Sora gets to PAUSE between those states. the whole rest of the episode he''s just being yanked from one to the other with no warning. that''s why it works.

...okay I''m gonna go eat dinner now, my brain is full.', '2013-10-06T09:48:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 92, 'QuietWatcher_X', 'av-day01', 'Newbie', 4, true, 'posting from the depths of my 4-year lurker status: this thread is the most fun I''ve had reading anime forums since 2010. you all are special.

signed,
a lurker who will return to the shadows after this.', '2013-10-06T10:01:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 93, 'AbigailFanAlready', 'av-abigailfan', 'Member', 504, true, 'Abigail vs Miyuki rivalry is going to be the SHOW. they didn''t even share a frame in ep 1. I''m already in for whatever the show does with that.

Abigail: cool, funny, relatable, loyal, [b]best girl of 2013[/b] — calling it now and locking it in.
Miyuki: theatrical, controlled, runs an entire student council squad, weaponizes essays.

completely opposite energy. Abigail is the friend you want at your back, Miyuki is the rival you want across the lobby. they''re gonna meet in ep 4 or 5, I''d bet money on it. and one of them is going to break.', '2013-10-06T10:14:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 94, 'GunKata_Saturn12', 'av-okamoto', 'Member', 422, true, '[quote=Crucible_Igniter_42 — #66 (page 4)]TEAM GRAYSON. I''ll die on this hill.[/quote]

[quote=MetaCode_Maximus — #76 (page 4)]TEAM SORA. and yeah Abigail''s finisher is sick. but Sora made the finisher POSSIBLE.[/quote]

stumbled on this debate from page 4. excuse me while I read 30 posts.

...OK CAUGHT UP. [b]both of y''all need to PAUSE.[/b]

@Crucible_Igniter_42 you''re right that Grayson carried the middle of the fight tactically. respect.
@MetaCode_Maximus you''re right that Sora''s character arc made the fight possible. respect.

now stop talking. [b]it''s TEAM ABIGAIL time[/b] and I''m putting receipts on the table because I am not letting either of you walk out of this thread with a W.

and I''m not saying that as a shipping meme or "best girl" noise. I''m saying it because Eden is clearly refusing the default action-anime arrangement where the boys drive the fight and the girls react prettily from the side. [b]We''re not doing "male dominate, female support."[/b] not with this storyboard. not with this shot priority. not with Abigail getting the kill card.

let''s actually break down what Abigail did. because she did NOT "show up at the end and take the cleanup." that''s an INSULT to what''s on screen. let me prove it.

[b]1.[/b] she SAW Sora turn back. she SAW Grayson peel off to help Ben with the cart. she SAW Sora''s 1v1 with YAMAGA happening. she chose to LAUNCH from the moving cart that Grayson was driving for two minutes. read that again. she JUMPED OFF a moving vehicle in the middle of a war zone to back up a teammate. no hesitation. no setup line. she just SENT IT.

[b]2.[/b] her launch is one of the cleanest aerial transitions in the entire episode. flame guns grapple hook fires OFF-SCREEN first — you HEAR the bang before you see her — gas line venting in a sharp downward burst that reads as a tiny silhouette, full body rotation through the camera-whip, THREE independent motion layers (body, hair, uniform) all individually drawn instead of cel-shifted as one block. this is hand-drawn key animator showoff work. one continuous unbroken cut from launch to land. that''s not "the cleanup." that''s a sakuga signature moment.

[b]3.[/b] her finisher is a continuous unbroken cut from hook-plant to kill. NO cheat-cuts. plant the hook on the open body, dive in, slash with flame guns blades at NEAR-CONTACT range, blade glow custom-colored gold-orange (deliberately different from Grayson''s red-orange so the audience can read who''s killing who in the chaos), continuous overlapping slash arcs instead of standard impact stamps. YAMAGA''s machine armor EXPLODES. BOOOM. red blood explodes out of the body. center-frame "[b]K.O![/b]" text. nobody else got a kill cam like that. she made YAMAGA [i]literally detonate[/i].

[b]4.[/b] THE NECKLACE CLUTCH DURING THE FALL. mid-air. subconscious grab. lands BADLY because the storyboard chose realism over heroism. dirt in her hair. uses the hook tension to yank herself around but can''t find an area, so she just ROLLS onto the ground. then she NOTICES the necklace is still there and exhales relief. "[i]...How did that happen?[/i]" delivered like she didn''t expect it to work. she COMMITTED to the finisher without knowing it would land. that''s not "cleanup." [b]that''s a leap of faith made in real time.[/b]

so let''s correct the record:

[list]
[*]Grayson fought the middle of the fight. he didn''t take the kill because he set up the squad.
[*]Sora fought the HEART of the fight. he set up the kill with raw spite.
[*][b]Abigail LED the ending of the fight.[/b] she didn''t "assist." she made the decisive choice, jumped off a moving cart, performed the cleanest sakuga sequence of the episode, made YAMAGA''s body literally detonate, AND committed to the move not knowing if she''d survive the landing.
[/list]

@Crucible_Igniter_42 chess work doesn''t kill YAMAGA. chess work POSITIONS YAMAGA. she KILLED him.
@MetaCode_Maximus Sora set it up, true. but the finisher is what BURST chose to put their best key animator on. you can SEE the production hours in the cut. that''s where the studio decided "this is the moment we are proud of."

the show literally TOLD YOU the answer with the shot list. Grayson''s fight is wide-shot tactical choreography (cool). Sora''s fight is mid-shot earn-the-hit progression (great). Abigail''s kill is a CENTER-FRAME one-cut sakuga showcase with on-screen "K.O!" text and an explosion. the camera told you which moment Burst wanted you to remember.

and zoom out from the fight for two seconds: Miyuki gets the thesis speech. Nova gets the ominous "It''s over" adult-world gravity. Likko gets a full-body comedy animation beat in four seconds. Echo is introduced through movement instead of posing. Abigail gets the finisher. Eden is building its female cast as engines, not ornaments. girls are not being carried by the plot. they are carrying the plot''s pressure points.

that''s why [b]TEAM ABIGAIL[/b] matters. it''s not only "who looked coolest." it''s the show proving its women can lead action, comedy, authority, horror, emotional restraint, and narrative payoff. maybe more than the men. maybe that''s the whole point. and honestly? good. let them lead.

[b]TEAM ABIGAIL.[/b] coffin shut. mic dropped. necklace clutched. I''m putting flowers on YAMAGA284''s grave.

(I am open to a TEAM TIE answer mechanically. but thematically? no. Abigail had the CLEANEST moment of the three and the girls are the core of this episode. that''s the non-negotiable.)', '2013-10-06T10:26:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 95, 'SakugaThreadZero', 'av-zeroframe', 'Database Contributor', 5894, true, 'got a few requests in PMs so I''m posting Miyuki''s full lobby speech here for the database. this is the actual transcript pass, not a fan TL. corrections welcome but I''m fairly confident on this one:

[quote="Miyuki Kagemitsu — pre-Void Rift lobby speech, ep 1"]"[b]No fear, no hesitation, no regrets![/b]
[b]If the walls above stand in front of you, advance to crush them![/b]
[b]Restrictions behind history are merely an excuse to refuse living![/b]
[b]That is the real truth of humanity![/b]
[b]Because of our mistakes, we deserve a path to choose where we keep moving forward![/b]
[b]Therefore, our choice towards history is REFUSAL![/b]"[/quote]

I need everyone to understand: this is what gets BOOMED out IN THE LOBBY before anyone has even fought a boss. no buildup. no flashback. no slow camera push-in. she just delivers it — framing tight, music dropped to silence underneath, her voice swelling on every line break — and then immediately picks Void Rift like none of it cost her anything.

that "[i]our choice towards history is refusal[/i]" line is the show''s thesis statement. mark it. that''s going to be the line of the season.

Saori Hayami doing performance of the year already. and ep 2 hasn''t even aired.', '2013-10-06T10:36:00Z', 'JST', '2013-10-06T10:48:00Z', 'cleaned up line breaks, added timestamp note (speech runs from 17:42 to 18:09 in the broadcast cut)', false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 96, 'CipherCaramel_Cyberpunk', 'av-guestcone', 'Member', 261, true, 'okay take with me here:

what if the SCHOOL is the simulation, not Planetation?

think about it. the school has UI overlays. the homeroom teacher is a "SYSTEM OVERRIDE". the propaganda posters are written like in-game tooltips. the riot has impact frames like a game. the vending machine has combat logs.

the VR helmet boot-up at home is going from one simulation INTO another. it''s nested. the cold open with the baby is the only "real" world.

I''m half-joking. half. that other half is dead serious.', '2013-10-06T10:52:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 97, 'ShounenLifer_VHS', 'av-vhssamurai', 'Anime Addict', 4191, true, '[quote=CipherCaramel_Cyberpunk;96]what if the SCHOOL is the simulation, not Planetation?[/quote]

hot. annoyingly hot. I don''t think it''s that, BUT the show is letting you read it that way. the UI overlays in the school are the SAME visual language as Planetation''s HUD. so even if school is "real", Sora''s experience of school is being filtered through gameplay logic.

that might be the show''s actual thesis. "what does it mean to grow up when your real life looks like a video game and your video game looks more real than school?"

congrats CipherCaramel_Cyberpunk you might have just outdone the storm-is-Sora theory for thread MVP. and that''s saying something.', '2013-10-06T11:08:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 98, 'Donut_Punisher', 'av-toonblock', 'Newbie', 2, true, '[quote=GunKata_Saturn12 — #94 (this page)]Eden is building its female cast as engines, not ornaments.[/quote]

THIS. this is what I''ve been trying to say since page 1 but didn''t have the words.

look at the girls in ep 1 and tell me they''re "supporting" anything:

[list]
[*][b]Abigail[/b] ends the bloodiest fight of the premiere and gets the only full kill-card moment.
[*][b]Miyuki[/b] owns the lobby with the thesis speech before the boys even understand the scale of the game.
[*][b]Nova[/b] turns KO HQ from office comedy into "oh the world is actually doomed" with two calm lines.
[*][b]Likko[/b] makes the whole lobby feel alive with one emote-spam beat and still comes off like future chaos royalty.
[*][b]Echo[/b] is introduced through parkour and dual blades, not beauty-shot posing. motion first, character first.
[*][b]Lisa and Sarah[/b] survive the hallway riot by being sharper than half the room and funnier than most of the boys.
[/list]

that''s not "male leads, female support." that''s an ensemble where the girls are carrying the thesis, the action punctuation, the political rival energy, the adult-world dread, AND the comedy texture.

so yeah. TEAM ABIGAIL for the YAMAGA fight, but bigger than that: [b]TEAM EDEN GIRLS LEADING THE SHOW.[/b] let the boys catch up.', '2013-10-06T11:21:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
