  ('ioe-ep1', 138, 'ShounenLifer_VHS', 'av-vhssamurai', 'Anime Addict', 4194, false, 'we need to retire the idea that the girls are supporting the boys here Miyuki owns the thesis speech Nova owns the dread Likko owns the lobby''s energy Echo owns motion Abigail owns the YAMAGA kill that''s five different kinds of leadership in one premiere the boys are important, but the women are the structure holding the episode''s biggest turns together frfr', '2013-10-06T22:07:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 139, 'YAMAGA284_Survivor', 'av-guestink', 'Newbie', 339, true, 'the parallel between miyuki''s thesis speech & nova''s "we have to take a stand" line is intentional they''re delivered in different rooms by different chars at different moments but they are saying the same thing in different registers miyuki: poetic, defiant, philosophical nova: flat, exhausted, professional same moral spine, two voices eden just gave the show''s central message to two women back to back & ppl are still calling them "side cast" read the episode', '2013-10-06T22:17:00Z', 'GMT', null, null, false, 'archived'),
