easily one of the best premiere episodes of 2013!', '2013-10-07T17:11:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 323, 'MunchyRollLagger', 'av-3eprule', 'Newbie', 697, true, 'Mariya Ise as Sora is such a good casting choice! Sora sounds genuinely 12 w/o being annoying, and his energy during the fight scene felt so scrappy and real 10/10 voice work lol', '2013-10-07T17:16:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 324, 'DesuKawaii_92', 'av-guestink', 'Member', 385, false, 'A few thoughts on ep 1 after my second watch:

- The weapon designs r amazing. Grayson using twin Crucible greatswords to herd YAMAGA into Sora''s attack path was brilliant squad tactics.
- Ben is pure comedic relief, disabling his safety governors immediately XD
- Studio Burst''s animation and sound design in the lobby scene was so atmospheric.

Bring on ep 2 next Sunday!', '2013-10-07T17:20:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 325, 'EpisodeOneOnLoop', 'av-moonlitpixel', 'Newbie', 751, false, 'the way Burst handles the FIVE FEMALE LEADS together vs separately is also smart. in the lobby they read as a UNIT (Council 1, full squad framing). in the field they read as individuals (Echo parkour, Likko taunting, Miyuki commanding). neither mode reduces them. they can be a coordinated team OR distinct individuals depending on what the scene needs. that''s range. that''s structure. that''s the OPPOSITE of "interchangeable side girls."', '2013-10-07T17:26:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
