  ('ioe-ep1', 362, 'ChibiComet_92', 'av-chibicomet', 'Forum Regular', 1124, false, '[quote="Originally posted earlier in thread"]3EpisodeRule retirement[/quote]

@3episoderule we all see you. you absolutely have not retired.', '2013-10-07T20:15:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 363, 'TokuFanMango', 'av-robomango', 'Forum Regular', 932, false, 'Echo Desmond is animated entirely in motion. her whole lobby intro is parkour between two training rails while testing dual blades. she NEVER stops moving. & the parkour is drawn cleanly — real weight transfer, real momentum, no impossible mid-air poses to make her look graceful. she''s drawn like an athlete. that''s Takuya writing women with bodies that actually function, not bodies posed for the camera.', '2013-10-07T20:18:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 364, 'CipherCaramel_Cyberpunk', 'av-ciphercaramel', 'Member', 283, false, 'mariya ise as sora is such a good casting choice! sora sounds genuinely 12 without being annoying, and his energy during the fight scene felt so scrappy and real. 10/10 voice work.', '2013-10-07T20:24:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 365, 'WaifuTaxIntern', 'av-zeroframe', 'Newbie', 165, true, '@OkamotoAcolyte the part of your post I keep coming back to is "the show is HOARDING firepower for later eps" because YES you don''t put Satou + Shimono + Kamiya + Sakura in a squad in ep 1 and not give that squad a 2-episode arc later somebody put me in cryo until those eps air', '2013-10-07T20:28:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 366, 'ShounenLifer_VHS', 'av-vhssamurai', 'Anime Addict', 4213, true, 'Miyuki Kagemitsu has only been on screen for 4 minutes and she already gave the most intimidating speech of the season ''Restrictions behind history r merely an excuse to refuse living!'' Saori Hayami delivered that line with pure authority <3', '2013-10-07T20:33:00Z', 'PDT', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 367, 'ShadowToast', 'av-shadowtoast', 'Member', 154, true, 'the most under-discussed thing in this thread: Miyuki''s [b]Zantetsuken[/b] stance. she''s holding a katana the size of her body in a guard stance & Burst animated her POSTURE to read as easy. not strained. not tense. EASY. like she has carried that weapon for years. that''s a body-language flex. a lazy studio would have animated her struggling with it for sympathy. Burst said no, she''s a swordswoman, draw her like one. respect...', '2013-10-07T20:36:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 368, '3EpisodeRule', 'av-3eprule', 'Senior Member', 1539, false, 'the parallel between miyuki''s thesis speech and nova''s "we have to take a stand" line is intentional. they''re delivered in different rooms by different characters at different moments but they are saying the same thing in different registers. miyuki: poetic, defiant, philosophical. nova: flat, exhausted, professional. same moral spine, two voices. eden just gave the show''s central message to two women back to back. and people are still calling them "side cast." read the ep... fr lol', '2013-10-07T20:40:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 369, 'NodeCoreCollector', 'av-rawrxd', 'Newbie', 278, false, 'ABIGAIL SAKUGA APPRECIATION POST. the moment after Sora softens YAMAGA up. wait for the music cue. then Abigail comes IN FROM OFFSCREEN with the Flame Guns grapple, fires both pistols at angle while still mid-air, slams the grapple anchor into YAMAGA''s shoulder, swings UP, lands ON him, finishes him with the flame guns at point blank — ENTIRE move, one continuous unbroken cut. that''s hand-animated ''studio shows off'' frames. Burst really said ''we''re new, here''s our resume.'' freeze any frame, all of them read.', '2013-10-07T20:45:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 370, 'HyperNekoMimi', 'av-hyperneko', 'Forum Regular', 514, true, 'My current theory for the show: the storm in Planetation isn''t just an in-game weather hazard, it''s connected to the blue egg from the cold open. The World Tree pulse in the opening scene was definitely a warning sign o_O', '2013-10-07T20:49:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
