  ('ioe-ep1', 446, 'PlanetationBro', 'av-bluesoda', 'Senior Member', 1942, false, 'teh burst step itself is good but teh CHARGE up to it is teh sakuga moment teh MetaCode plates breaking apart, teh inner glow building, Sora''s stance dropping low, teh camera tightening on his arm for one extra frame — that''s all anticipation animation, and it''s teh reason teh burst step lands as hard as it does anticipation is half of sakuga and Burst gets it', '2013-10-08T02:06:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 447, 'GoldenSloth_Animu', 'av-goldensloth', 'Newbie', 33, false, 'grayson using dual greatswords with remote ignition mode was badass >_>', '2013-10-08T02:10:00Z', 'JST', '2013-10-08T03:06:00Z', 'added thought', false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 448, 'EdenStan', 'av-robomango', 'Member', 491, false, 'rewatched episode 1 w/ friends tonight the pacing in this premiere is so well done:

1 the cold open immediately sets up a creepy mystery w/ the blue egg under the world tree.
2 the school and lobby scenes introduce the main crew (sora, grayson, abigail, ben) naturally without long boring info-dumps.
3 the yamaga284 fight delivers top-tier action sakuga, and miyuki''s speech at the end sets up the stakes for the whole show.

easily one of the best premiere episodes of 2013!', '2013-10-08T02:14:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 449, 'NodeCoreOmega', 'av-nodeomega', 'Senior Member', 2919, true, 'appreciation for [b]kana hanazawa as abigail.[/b] hanazawa is famous for soft-spoken, vulnerable, often shy roles abigail is the opposite of that she''s confident, dry, deadpan, action-first hanazawa is playing against type and she''s nailing it that''s the kind of casting burst could have played safe with by hiring a more typecast "strong girl" va they didn''t they trusted hanazawa to expand her range and she''s doing it [b]best girl of 2013[/b] is going to age incredibly well', '2013-10-08T02:18:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 450, 'FillerEpisodeFan', 'av-nekotoast', 'Senior Member', 665, true, 'okay can we just establish the canonical women-of-eden-ep-1 ranking really quick? not best-girl. not waifu ranking. but "who got the most lead-level screen time and respect." my list, in order of impact: 1) miyuki (thesis speech, lobby authority). 2) abigail (yamaga finisher, hoodie calm). 3) nova (it''s over, moral spine). 4) echo (parkour intro, vp staging). 5) likko (chaos lobby comedy, shotgun taunt). 6) lisa (riot diagnosis). 7) sarah (crisis management). all seven are doing real character work. seven. in one ep. ngl', '2013-10-08T02:22:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 451, 'HellsKitchenAnimu', 'av-kitchenstar', 'Forum Regular', 567, true, 'rewatched epside 1 w/ friends tonight. teh pacing in this premiere is so well done:

