  ('ioe-ep1', 711, 'MoshiMoshi_2007', 'av-cyberlunchbox', 'Newbie', 647, true, 'burst animated [b]abigail walking through the school riot w/ her hands in her hoodie pockets[/b]. i cannot stress this enough. the chaos breaks around her body. she doesn''t react. she doesn''t grab a weapon. she just moves through it like the storm doesn''t apply to her. that staging choice taught us before the yamaga fight that abigail is the un-rattle-able one. and then the storyboard followed through by giving her the k.o. shot. setup → payoff at the char-design level. that''s the takuya pipeline doing its job.', '2013-10-08T17:35:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep1', 712, 'SubsOverDubs4Life', 'av-3eprule', 'Newbie', 685, false, 'Rewatched Episode 1 w/ friends tonight. teh pacing in this premiere is so well done:

1. teh cold open immediately sets up a creepy mystery w/ teh blue egg under teh World Tree.
2. teh school and lobby scenes introduce teh main crew (Sora, gray, Abigail, Ben) naturally without long boring info-dumps.
3. teh YAMAGA284 fight delivers top-tier action sakuga, and miyku''s speech at teh end sets up teh stakes for teh whole show.

Easily one of teh best premiere episodes of 2013!', '2013-10-08T17:38:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
