  ('ioe-ep3', 498, 'VoidRift_Survivor', 'av-zeroframe', 'Newbie', 108, true, 'The dialogue between Abigail and Miyuki was savage: ''Miyuki, it''s been 6 years and you''re still hurting everyone!'' / ''And that''s the problem! You''re acting as if there are rights to rebel against authority!'' / ''Do not tell me what to do, you lower caste pig!''', '2013-10-21T01:57:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 499, 'LisaSniperQueen', 'av-kappazero', 'Member', 48, true, 'Kana Hanazawa and Saori Hayami giving the performances of their careers. When Abigail caught Zantenzetsuken between both Flame Gun frames, slid inside Miyuki''s guard, and delivered that heavy spin-kick that made Miyuki''s forearm visibly shake from adrenaline and pain?! That''s the first time Miyuki''s perfect ice-queen composure broke!', '2013-10-22T10:49:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 500, 'NovaFanPixel', 'av-moonlitpixel', 'Database Contributor', 6263, true, 'Look at the weight in Sora''s landing when Ben launches him in — he hits the ground, tucks into a combat roll, pushes right back up to his feet without losing speed, and charges Nero head-on. Sora''s scrappy physical combat style is so satisfying to watch!', '2013-10-20T04:51:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 501, 'EchoDesmond_Loyalist', 'av-kappazero', 'Newbie', 65, true, 'Kagura holding back the Crucible flames until the very end — hands and kicks win the space, Crucibles cash out the damage! That Red Divide cut splitting the corridor in two with that delayed three-frame impact hold... Kagura is an animation god.', '2013-10-21T06:06:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 502, 'NekoToast92', 'av-nekotoast', 'Forum Regular', 944, true, 'Klaus saying ''I''m calling in Nova so that egg doesn''t destroy the damn continent''... NOVA IS BACK NEXT WEEK!! Remember her quote in Ep 1 about moral standing? Peak hype!', '2013-10-23T10:59:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 503, 'Grayson_Ignition_DualBlades', 'av-3eprule', 'Newbie', 87, true, 'The animation when Sora realizes flash-stepping is a trap and takes that ordinary, slow, human step? ''Nero''s prediction was perfect. That was why it failed. It predicted the Sora who had already panicked.'' Burst''s storyboarders understand pacing on a fundamental level.', '2013-10-22T23:41:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 504, 'GraysonRothenbergStan', 'av-kitchenstar', 'Newbie', 111, true, 'Echo Desmond with that ridiculous Anchor Armament — switching from dual blades to twin rotary machine guns and then locking them into that massive double-edged Anchor Greatsword! And pausing mid-fight just to insult Lisa''s shoes: ''I''m staring at how UGLY your shoes look'' — ''Nobody cares! Garbage!!'' Then ending in a mutual double drop-kick where both girls get sent flying!', '2013-10-22T14:37:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 505, 'ArthurWhiteCommander', 'av-millenniumfan', 'Newbie', 80, true, 'The kinetic animation when Ben throws Sora toward Nero: Sora falls into the ground hard, but rolls through the dirt to absorb the shock, immediately pushes back up, and charges straight into Nero! It''s not comedic relief — you feel the raw momentum, grit, and tenacity of him refusing to stay down.', '2013-10-20T02:07:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 506, 'EchoDesmond_Loyalist', 'av-robomango', 'Newbie', 131, true, 'The sound design on Echo''s Anchor Greatsword connecting with the fossil arch was deafening. You can feel the sheer kinetic weight in Burst''s sound mixing.', '2013-10-22T03:57:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 507, 'ImageboardGoblin', 'av-forumgoblin', 'Member', 462, true, 'Sora vs Nero was a psychological battle disguised as an action sequence. Nero''s 3-lane route grid (blue = move, yellow = delay, red = punish) wasn''t just a boss gimmick; Nero was literally reading player psychology. He counted on Sora''s shounen instinct to rush in whenever someone yelled.', '2013-10-22T13:28:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 508, 'GraysonRothenbergStan', 'av-cyberlunchbox', 'Newbie', 97, true, 'Echo Desmond with that ridiculous Anchor Armament — switching from dual blades to twin rotary machine guns and then locking them into that massive double-edged Anchor Greatsword! And pausing mid-fight just to insult Lisa''s shoes: ''I''m staring at how UGLY your shoes look'' — ''Nobody cares! Garbage!!'' Then ending in a mutual double drop-kick where both girls get sent flying!', '2013-10-22T20:20:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 509, 'NovaFanPixel', 'av-moonlitpixel', 'Database Contributor', 6272, true, 'Action Director Kagura completely reinvented anime swordplay in Grayson vs IgniteCOD_Clutch. Look at the keyframes: when Ignite tries to slide, Grayson doesn''t swing a sword — he drops his hips and stamps a stiff low kick into the knee! Then a lead jab to check the SMG reload, and that brutal axe kick crashing down straight through the build panel! It''s actual boxing and Muay Thai mechanics instead of floaty anime sword-flailing!', '2013-10-21T12:18:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 510, 'likko-chwangun213', 'av-sakurastatic', 'Forum Regular', 767, true, 'Kagura holding back the Crucible flames until the very end — hands and kicks win the space, Crucibles cash out the damage! That Red Divide cut splitting the corridor in two with that delayed three-frame impact hold... Kagura is an animation god.', '2013-10-21T11:47:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 511, 'AbigailFanAlready', 'av-abigailfan', 'Member', 562, true, 'Preview quote: ''There will be an investigation of the source to ensure the safety of the other game world''s... Country!'' Next episode: SOUL ANCHOR!', '2013-10-23T09:44:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 512, 'BostonBaka_Gaijin', 'av-bostonbean', 'Member', 360, true, 'Emiko calling Arthur White ''Whitie~ You there~?'' in the post-credits scene! She''s the acting CEO of FRM while casually walking a fashion show in Shell 2?! The lore rabbit hole goes so deep.', '2013-10-19T20:52:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 513, 'Zantenzetsuken_Cutter', 'av-zeroframe', 'Newbie', 50, true, 'Kaito Ishikawa''s vocal delivery on ''HERE''S YOUR L!'' gave me actual goosebumps. And then slamming Maxino through two fossil ribs down into the ridge! When Ben faceplanted in the dirt murmuring ''Scientific reaction...'' and then hit his engine with a wrench: ''You''ve got five more minutes in you. That wasn''t a question.'' What a legendary bro!', '2013-10-22T09:36:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 514, 'Zantenzetsuken_Cutter', 'av-toonblock', 'Newbie', 60, true, 'Abigail vs Miyuki was so raw and personal. Zero graceful tournament rules — just six years of hatred exploding on screen.', '2013-10-21T02:22:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 515, 'Grayson_Ignition_DualBlades', 'av-millenniumfan', 'Member', 130, true, 'Grayson walking Ignite down through bullets with Gojo spacing arrogance and Ichigo forward pressure was pure aura. He didn''t even run. Just steady, terrifying forward footsteps until Ignite had nowhere left to jump.', '2013-10-23T10:24:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 516, 'CipherCaramel_Cyberpunk', 'av-ciphercaramel', 'Member', 293, true, 'Look at the weight in Sora''s landing when Ben launches him in — he hits the ground, tucks into a combat roll, pushes right back up to his feet without losing speed, and charges Nero head-on. Sora''s scrappy physical combat style is so satisfying to watch!', '2013-10-23T14:14:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 517, 'Andreas_VectorUplink', 'av-robomango', 'Newbie', 24, true, 'Minko Abercrombie losing arguments with physics was the comedic highlight of the year. Tripping on her own shoes, sliding down a hill on her stomach, screaming ''I meant to do that!... I didn''t mean to do that!'' while accidentally deflecting Likko''s shotgun shells with her scythe!', '2013-10-20T10:43:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 518, 'HyperNekoMimi', 'av-hyperneko', 'Forum Regular', 526, true, 'THAT CLIFFHANGER IS EVIL. Margo drops the blue device, Andreas screams ''Grayson, don''t land there!'', and the whole battlefield literally folds like paper into a black hole?!', '2013-10-21T04:25:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 519, 'EchoDesmond_Loyalist', 'av-3eprule', 'Newbie', 77, true, 'Grayson''s reaction to getting smacked by Minko''s scythe: ''Don''t do that again.'' Minko: ''Okay!''... the comedic timing between Okamoto and Minko''s VA is unmatched.', '2013-10-22T02:22:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 520, 'sleepySenpai_DesuKa', 'av-sleepysenpai', 'Member', 420, true, 'The animation when Sora realizes flash-stepping is a trap and takes that ordinary, slow, human step? ''Nero''s prediction was perfect. That was why it failed. It predicted the Sora who had already panicked.'' Burst''s storyboarders understand pacing on a fundamental level.', '2013-10-22T10:57:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 521, 'AbigailFlameRush', 'av-calsparrow', 'Newbie', 32, true, 'Ben Smythe is the absolute MVP of this episode. Maxino triggering that 45-second Grand Finale countdown with the entire floor lighting up in red and gold firework fuse lines was insane.', '2013-10-20T10:47:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 522, 'likko-chwangun213', 'av-sakurastatic', 'Forum Regular', 775, true, 'Kagura holding back the Crucible flames until the very end — hands and kicks win the space, Crucibles cash out the damage! That Red Divide cut splitting the corridor in two with that delayed three-frame impact hold... Kagura is an animation god.', '2013-10-20T01:32:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 523, 'EmikoFashionQueen', 'av-hyperneko', 'Newbie', 131, true, 'Sora leaping out of the cart, spinning into a high-speed MetaCode Beyblade into Kieran and William, but explicitly avoiding Echo and Miyuki because ''I respect women''??? Bro is 12 years old and already a gentleman XD', '2013-10-20T14:58:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 524, 'BenSmytheGaming', 'av-hyperneko', 'Member', 69, true, 'The choreography on Grayson''s spinning back kick anticipating Ignite''s purple vow teleport exit... you can see the anticipation frames where Grayson rotates his hips before Ignite even materializes. That is high-level action direction.', '2013-10-22T01:34:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 525, 'Grayson_Ignition_DualBlades', 'av-day01', 'Member', 123, true, 'The sound design on Echo''s Anchor Greatsword connecting with the fossil arch was deafening. You can feel the sheer kinetic weight in Burst''s sound mixing.', '2013-10-20T12:14:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 526, 'IgniteCOD_Sweat', 'av-luckynoodle', 'Member', 118, true, 'Action Director Kagura completely reinvented anime swordplay in Grayson vs IgniteCOD_Clutch. Look at the keyframes: when Ignite tries to slide, Grayson doesn''t swing a sword — he drops his hips and stamps a stiff low kick into the knee! Then a lead jab to check the SMG reload, and that brutal axe kick crashing down straight through the build panel! It''s actual boxing and Muay Thai mechanics instead of floaty anime sword-flailing!', '2013-10-19T23:49:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 527, 'BenSmytheGaming', 'av-luckynoodle', 'Member', 90, true, 'Ben didn''t even try to dodge at the end. At 96% heat, he literally ran straight through overlapping blast zones, ate the explosion point-blank with sparks and blood flying everywhere, and rammed that spinning NodeCore drill right through Maxino''s guard roaring ''HERE''S YOUR L!''', '2013-10-20T12:27:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 528, 'NodeCorePilot', 'av-mecharonin', 'Senior Member', 2254, true, 'Ben Smythe is the absolute MVP of this episode. Maxino triggering that 45-second Grand Finale countdown with the entire floor lighting up in red and gold firework fuse lines was insane.', '2013-10-20T06:46:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 529, 'GraysonRothenbergStan', 'av-ciphercaramel', 'Newbie', 71, true, 'The dialogue between Abigail and Miyuki was savage: ''Miyuki, it''s been 6 years and you''re still hurting everyone!'' / ''And that''s the problem! You''re acting as if there are rights to rebel against authority!'' / ''Do not tell me what to do, you lower caste pig!''', '2013-10-22T01:55:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 530, 'ScientificReactionsBro', 'av-luckynoodle', 'Newbie', 59, true, 'Likko running down the wall like an elegant classical ballerina with her rhythm shotgun to fast piano music (''4e corde! Tempo miracle ultra-rapide!'')... only for Minko to get caught in the route wheel, spin 360 degrees, get catapulted across the canyon into a tree, chase the cart on foot, and whack Grayson in the back of the head with her scythe handle: ''OW! DAMMIT, MINKO!''', '2013-10-22T21:25:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 531, 'RetroBluRay_AMV', 'av-retrobluray', 'Forum Regular', 1471, true, 'Maxino was such a cool boss design. The firework cylinders strapped to his rig, throwing smoke canisters and using gold blast zones to launch Ben into traps... but Ben turning the launch blast into aerial momentum with Flight Mode was galaxy-brain play.', '2013-10-22T06:28:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 532, 'TokuFanMango', 'av-robomango', 'Forum Regular', 954, true, 'The kinetic animation when Ben throws Sora toward Nero: Sora falls into the ground hard, but rolls through the dirt to absorb the shock, immediately pushes back up, and charges straight into Nero! It''s not comedic relief — you feel the raw momentum, grit, and tenacity of him refusing to stay down.', '2013-10-20T03:38:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 533, 'BenSmytheGaming', 'av-sakurastatic', 'Newbie', 15, true, 'Grayson walking Ignite down through bullets with Gojo spacing arrogance and Ichigo forward pressure was pure aura. He didn''t even run. Just steady, terrifying forward footsteps until Ignite had nowhere left to jump.', '2013-10-21T21:51:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 534, 'ImageboardGoblin', 'av-forumgoblin', 'Member', 462, true, 'Klaus saying ''I''m calling in Nova so that egg doesn''t destroy the damn continent''... NOVA IS BACK NEXT WEEK!! Remember her quote in Ep 1 about moral standing? Peak hype!', '2013-10-22T08:50:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 535, 'Andreas_VectorUplink', 'av-bostonbean', 'Newbie', 98, true, 'Miyuki Sawashiro''s ED ''24 Hours Everyday'' showing Abigail''s peaceful school routine vs her bleeding in the game... tears in my eyes. Such a beautiful, nostalgic song ;_;', '2013-10-23T09:48:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 536, 'Miyuki_Advance_HQ', 'av-okamoto', 'Member', 138, true, 'Minko Abercrombie losing arguments with physics was the comedic highlight of the year. Tripping on her own shoes, sliding down a hill on her stomach, screaming ''I meant to do that!... I didn''t mean to do that!'' while accidentally deflecting Likko''s shotgun shells with her scythe!', '2013-10-20T18:20:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 537, 'IgniteCOD_Sweat', 'av-nodeomega', 'Member', 121, true, 'The contrast between Grayson''s grounded boxing stance and IgniteCOD rage-typing in chat: ''??? Who the f---? Get off me!'' and ''Look at this, bitch!'' while dropping launch pads and quickscoping like an angry 14-year-old on Modern Warfare 2 is the greatest gaming comedy in anime history.', '2013-10-20T00:14:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 538, 'AbigailFanAlready', 'av-abigailfan', 'Member', 561, true, 'Sora shattering the route line under Nero''s boots, doing the cat-ears grin with the forehead ''L'' sign, whispering ''Later~'', and blitz-dashing away... pure scrappy protagonist brilliance :3', '2013-10-21T18:26:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 539, 'ArthurWhiteCommander', 'av-goldensloth', 'Member', 38, true, 'The whole sequence with the cart flying through the sky! Grayson white-knuckling the steering bar, Sora latching his red-white MetaCode threads onto the front axle to keep it level, Ben drilling through smoke, and Minko waving her scythe... Studio Burst created the most absurd yet epic war chariot in anime!', '2013-10-23T08:42:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 540, 'BurstAnimKid', 'av-luckynoodle', 'Member', 291, true, 'The animation when Sora realizes flash-stepping is a trap and takes that ordinary, slow, human step? ''Nero''s prediction was perfect. That was why it failed. It predicted the Sora who had already panicked.'' Burst''s storyboarders understand pacing on a fundamental level.', '2013-10-22T11:18:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 541, 'NekoToast92', 'av-nekotoast', 'Forum Regular', 933, true, 'Sora leaping out of the cart, spinning into a high-speed MetaCode Beyblade into Kieran and William, but explicitly avoiding Echo and Miyuki because ''I respect women''??? Bro is 12 years old and already a gentleman XD', '2013-10-21T03:50:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 542, 'RawrXD_2007', 'av-rawrxd', 'Member', 223, true, 'The choreography on Grayson''s spinning back kick anticipating Ignite''s purple vow teleport exit... you can see the anticipation frames where Grayson rotates his hips before Ignite even materializes. That is high-level action direction.', '2013-10-23T08:17:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived')
