  ('ioe-ep3', 623, 'HellsKitchenAnimu', 'av-kitchenstar', 'Forum Regular', 572, true, 'Action Director Kagura completely reinvented anime swordplay in Grayson vs IgniteCOD_Clutch. Look at the keyframes: when Ignite tries to slide, Grayson doesn''t swing a sword — he drops his hips and stamps a stiff low kick into the knee! Then a lead jab to check the SMG reload, and that brutal axe kick crashing down straight through the build panel! It''s actual boxing and Muay Thai mechanics instead of floaty anime sword-flailing!', '2013-10-20T02:23:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 624, 'PlanetationBro', 'av-bluesoda', 'Senior Member', 1965, true, 'The animation when Sora realizes flash-stepping is a trap and takes that ordinary, slow, human step? ''Nero''s prediction was perfect. That was why it failed. It predicted the Sora who had already panicked.'' Burst''s storyboarders understand pacing on a fundamental level.', '2013-10-19T19:20:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 625, 'RetroBluRay_AMV', 'av-retrobluray', 'Forum Regular', 1484, true, 'Abigail using Flame Gun recoil to kick herself sideways under Miyuki''s sonic shots was incredible comp work. The camera staying glued to her center of gravity while the background rotated into speed lines... peak sakuga.', '2013-10-23T03:58:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 626, 'ScientificReactionsBro', 'av-day01', 'Member', 72, true, 'Grayson''s reaction to getting smacked by Minko''s scythe: ''Don''t do that again.'' Minko: ''Okay!''... the comedic timing between Okamoto and Minko''s VA is unmatched.', '2013-10-21T09:37:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 627, 'HollowToast', 'av-hollowtoast', 'Senior Member', 2510, true, 'Echo Desmond with that ridiculous Anchor Armament — switching from dual blades to twin rotary machine guns and then locking them into that massive double-edged Anchor Greatsword! And pausing mid-fight just to insult Lisa''s shoes: ''I''m staring at how UGLY your shoes look'' — ''Nobody cares! Garbage!!'' Then ending in a mutual double drop-kick where both girls get sent flying!', '2013-10-22T09:31:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 628, 'Miyuki_Advance_HQ', 'av-shadowtoast', 'Newbie', 109, true, 'Maxino was such a cool boss design. The firework cylinders strapped to his rig, throwing smoke canisters and using gold blast zones to launch Ben into traps... but Ben turning the launch blast into aerial momentum with Flight Mode was galaxy-brain play.', '2013-10-20T09:40:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 629, 'BenSmytheGaming', 'av-kappazero', 'Newbie', 55, true, 'The whole sequence with the cart flying through the sky! Grayson white-knuckling the steering bar, Sora latching his red-white MetaCode threads onto the front axle to keep it level, Ben drilling through smoke, and Minko waving her scythe... Studio Burst created the most absurd yet epic war chariot in anime!', '2013-10-22T03:02:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 630, 'HollowToast', 'av-hollowtoast', 'Senior Member', 2496, true, 'Action Director Kagura completely reinvented anime swordplay in Grayson vs IgniteCOD_Clutch. Look at the keyframes: when Ignite tries to slide, Grayson doesn''t swing a sword — he drops his hips and stamps a stiff low kick into the knee! Then a lead jab to check the SMG reload, and that brutal axe kick crashing down straight through the build panel! It''s actual boxing and Muay Thai mechanics instead of floaty anime sword-flailing!', '2013-10-21T05:47:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 631, 'ArthurWhiteCommander', 'av-nodeomega', 'Member', 79, true, 'Kaito Ishikawa''s vocal delivery on ''HERE''S YOUR L!'' gave me actual goosebumps. And then slamming Maxino through two fossil ribs down into the ridge! When Ben faceplanted in the dirt murmuring ''Scientific reaction...'' and then hit his engine with a wrench: ''You''ve got five more minutes in you. That wasn''t a question.'' What a legendary bro!', '2013-10-21T18:12:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 632, 'Klaus_DeadpanEnjoyer', 'av-nekotoast', 'Newbie', 25, true, 'Sora shattering the route line under Nero''s boots, doing the cat-ears grin with the forehead ''L'' sign, whispering ''Later~'', and blitz-dashing away... pure scrappy protagonist brilliance :3', '2013-10-21T04:38:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 633, 'BenSmytheGaming', 'av-rawrxd', 'Newbie', 77, true, 'Ben Smythe is the absolute MVP of this episode. Maxino triggering that 45-second Grand Finale countdown with the entire floor lighting up in red and gold firework fuse lines was insane.', '2013-10-22T20:26:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 634, 'VoidRift_Survivor', 'av-day01', 'Member', 56, true, 'Maxino was such a cool boss design. The firework cylinders strapped to his rig, throwing smoke canisters and using gold blast zones to launch Ben into traps... but Ben turning the launch blast into aerial momentum with Flight Mode was galaxy-brain play.', '2013-10-21T04:14:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 635, 'EmikoFashionQueen', 'av-kappazero', 'Newbie', 90, true, 'Lisa Hoshino vs Echo Desmond was the most stylish, petty catfight of the decade. Lisa''s internal monologue: ''Don''t shoot the person. Shoot the step they need.'' followed by interrupting Margo''s sound cannon with ''You''re mine, pig!!'' — Rina Satou at her absolute best.', '2013-10-23T03:12:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 636, 'PressureChain_God', 'av-calsparrow', 'Newbie', 88, true, 'Kana Hanazawa and Saori Hayami giving the performances of their careers. When Abigail caught Zantenzetsuken between both Flame Gun frames, slid inside Miyuki''s guard, and delivered that heavy spin-kick that made Miyuki''s forearm visibly shake from adrenaline and pain?! That''s the first time Miyuki''s perfect ice-queen composure broke!', '2013-10-22T22:30:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 637, 'Nishikawa_OP_Hype', 'av-goldensloth', 'Newbie', 38, true, 'Lisa Hoshino vs Echo Desmond was the most stylish, petty catfight of the decade. Lisa''s internal monologue: ''Don''t shoot the person. Shoot the step they need.'' followed by interrupting Margo''s sound cannon with ''You''re mine, pig!!'' — Rina Satou at her absolute best.', '2013-10-21T23:48:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 638, 'Miyuki_Advance_HQ', 'av-rawrxd', 'Newbie', 104, true, 'Minko Abercrombie losing arguments with physics was the comedic highlight of the year. Tripping on her own shoes, sliding down a hill on her stomach, screaming ''I meant to do that!... I didn''t mean to do that!'' while accidentally deflecting Likko''s shotgun shells with her scythe!', '2013-10-22T21:55:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 639, 'ED_Appreciator', 'av-3eprule', 'Newbie', 114, true, 'The choreography on Grayson''s spinning back kick anticipating Ignite''s purple vow teleport exit... you can see the anticipation frames where Grayson rotates his hips before Ignite even materializes. That is high-level action direction.', '2013-10-20T07:32:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 640, 'NovaFanPixel', 'av-moonlitpixel', 'Database Contributor', 6279, true, 'The contrast between Grayson''s grounded boxing stance and IgniteCOD rage-typing in chat: ''??? Who the f---? Get off me!'' and ''Look at this, bitch!'' while dropping launch pads and quickscoping like an angry 14-year-old on Modern Warfare 2 is the greatest gaming comedy in anime history.', '2013-10-21T10:02:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 641, 'NeroRouteMaster', 'av-goldensloth', 'Newbie', 115, true, 'Look at the weight in Sora''s landing when Ben launches him in — he hits the ground, tucks into a combat roll, pushes right back up to his feet without losing speed, and charges Nero head-on. Sora''s scrappy physical combat style is so satisfying to watch!', '2013-10-21T05:52:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 642, 'NodeCorePilot', 'av-mecharonin', 'Senior Member', 2248, true, 'Echo Desmond with that ridiculous Anchor Armament — switching from dual blades to twin rotary machine guns and then locking them into that massive double-edged Anchor Greatsword! And pausing mid-fight just to insult Lisa''s shoes: ''I''m staring at how UGLY your shoes look'' — ''Nobody cares! Garbage!!'' Then ending in a mutual double drop-kick where both girls get sent flying!', '2013-10-23T04:40:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 643, 'Miyuki_Advance_HQ', 'av-vermilionowl', 'Newbie', 126, true, 'The animation when Sora realizes flash-stepping is a trap and takes that ordinary, slow, human step? ''Nero''s prediction was perfect. That was why it failed. It predicted the Sora who had already panicked.'' Burst''s storyboarders understand pacing on a fundamental level.', '2013-10-20T09:35:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 644, 'ImageboardGoblin', 'av-forumgoblin', 'Member', 471, true, 'Kagura holding back the Crucible flames until the very end — hands and kicks win the space, Crucibles cash out the damage! That Red Divide cut splitting the corridor in two with that delayed three-frame impact hold... Kagura is an animation god.', '2013-10-20T19:54:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 645, 'Grayson_Ignition_DualBlades', 'av-vermilionowl', 'Member', 41, true, 'Emiko calling Arthur White ''Whitie~ You there~?'' in the post-credits scene! She''s the acting CEO of FRM while casually walking a fashion show in Shell 2?! The lore rabbit hole goes so deep.', '2013-10-21T14:14:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 646, 'Klaus_DeadpanEnjoyer', 'av-robomango', 'Newbie', 92, true, 'Sora and Abigail reaching out for each other, their fingertips missing by two centimeters, and then the screen flashes white and EVERYONE GETS SUCKED IN?? Every single UI card reading SIGNAL LOST at once!', '2013-10-21T22:31:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 647, 'StormWallTheory', 'av-stormwalltheory', 'Senior Member', 3090, true, 'Kaito Ishikawa''s vocal delivery on ''HERE''S YOUR L!'' gave me actual goosebumps. And then slamming Maxino through two fossil ribs down into the ridge! When Ben faceplanted in the dirt murmuring ''Scientific reaction...'' and then hit his engine with a wrench: ''You''ve got five more minutes in you. That wasn''t a question.'' What a legendary bro!', '2013-10-20T06:38:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 648, 'GraysonRothenbergStan', 'av-sakurastatic', 'Newbie', 49, true, 'Kaito Ishikawa''s vocal delivery on ''HERE''S YOUR L!'' gave me actual goosebumps. And then slamming Maxino through two fossil ribs down into the ridge! When Ben faceplanted in the dirt murmuring ''Scientific reaction...'' and then hit his engine with a wrench: ''You''ve got five more minutes in you. That wasn''t a question.'' What a legendary bro!', '2013-10-22T18:22:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 649, 'Andreas_VectorUplink', 'av-nodeomega', 'Newbie', 73, true, 'Action Director Kagura completely reinvented anime swordplay in Grayson vs IgniteCOD_Clutch. Look at the keyframes: when Ignite tries to slide, Grayson doesn''t swing a sword — he drops his hips and stamps a stiff low kick into the knee! Then a lead jab to check the SMG reload, and that brutal axe kick crashing down straight through the build panel! It''s actual boxing and Muay Thai mechanics instead of floaty anime sword-flailing!', '2013-10-21T09:31:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 650, 'ArthurWhiteCommander', 'av-vermilionowl', 'Newbie', 26, true, 'The kinetic animation when Ben throws Sora toward Nero: Sora falls into the ground hard, but rolls through the dirt to absorb the shock, immediately pushes back up, and charges straight into Nero! It''s not comedic relief — you feel the raw momentum, grit, and tenacity of him refusing to stay down.', '2013-10-22T11:31:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 651, 'Nova_ContinentSaver', 'av-vermilionowl', 'Newbie', 66, true, 'The kinetic animation when Ben throws Sora toward Nero: Sora falls into the ground hard, but rolls through the dirt to absorb the shock, immediately pushes back up, and charges straight into Nero! It''s not comedic relief — you feel the raw momentum, grit, and tenacity of him refusing to stay down.', '2013-10-22T21:21:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 652, 'NodeCoreOmega', 'av-nodeomega', 'Senior Member', 2941, true, 'The sound design on Echo''s Anchor Greatsword connecting with the fossil arch was deafening. You can feel the sheer kinetic weight in Burst''s sound mixing.', '2013-10-23T13:11:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 653, 'Andreas_VectorUplink', 'av-okamoto', 'Member', 138, true, 'Action Director Kagura completely reinvented anime swordplay in Grayson vs IgniteCOD_Clutch. Look at the keyframes: when Ignite tries to slide, Grayson doesn''t swing a sword — he drops his hips and stamps a stiff low kick into the knee! Then a lead jab to check the SMG reload, and that brutal axe kick crashing down straight through the build panel! It''s actual boxing and Muay Thai mechanics instead of floaty anime sword-flailing!', '2013-10-20T05:18:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 654, 'Grayson_Ignition_DualBlades', 'av-bostonbean', 'Newbie', 118, true, 'Ben didn''t even try to dodge at the end. At 96% heat, he literally ran straight through overlapping blast zones, ate the explosion point-blank with sparks and blood flying everywhere, and rammed that spinning NodeCore drill right through Maxino''s guard roaring ''HERE''S YOUR L!''', '2013-10-19T23:17:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 655, 'MaxinoDemolitionFan', 'av-rawrxd', 'Newbie', 29, true, 'Abigail using Flame Gun recoil to kick herself sideways under Miyuki''s sonic shots was incredible comp work. The camera staying glued to her center of gravity while the background rotated into speed lines... peak sakuga.', '2013-10-20T12:53:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
  ('ioe-ep3', 656, 'Nova_ContinentSaver', 'av-sakurastatic', 'Member', 36, true, 'Emiko calling Arthur White ''Whitie~ You there~?'' in the post-credits scene! She''s the acting CEO of FRM while casually walking a fashion show in Shell 2?! The lore rabbit hole goes so deep.', '2013-10-22T20:47:00Z', 'JST', null, null, false, 'archived'),
